        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="notes">
      <p>For people new to local models: the processor matters less than the size and speed of the memory the model can use.</p>
      <p>At 4 bits, a model takes about 0.6 GB per billion parameters, plus space for the context. These are my own chat models as 4-bit GGUF files.</p>
      <p>The operating system also needs memory. On a 16 GB machine, keep the model under about 10 GB.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </Slide>

  <Slide section="Hardware" label="Memory bandwidth">
